# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Secrets / environment (keys are env-only by design; never commit them)
.env
.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# Logs, temp and OS noise
*.log
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Runtime artefacts: never commit case data, operational state or retrieval logs
business_pipeline_v0.12/business_pipeline/cases/
business_pipeline_v0.12/business_pipeline/state/
business_pipeline_v0.12/business_pipeline/retrieval_log.jsonl
business_pipeline_v0.12/business_pipeline/portfolios/

# The corpus: the owner's PDF library is a working collection, not source.
# It is 1.7 GB; the corpus records each document's path, hash and pages in
# corpus.sqlite, and that record is the thing that belongs in git.
DATABASE/

# Corpus runtime state: the database is rebuilt from the PDFs, the working
# copies are the PDFs, and the search index is disposable.
corpus-db/corpus.sqlite
corpus-db/pdfs/
corpus-db/meili/
corpus-db/data.ms/

# Word lock files
~$*.docx

# Scratch from a build session: one-off scripts and rendered page images
/_tmp_*.py
/_tmp_*.ps1
/_tmp_*.pdf
/page-*.png

# The Meilisearch program itself: a downloaded binary (114 MB), not source.
# GitHub refuses any file over 100 MB, and nothing needs it from git.
corpus-db/meilisearch.exe
corpus-db/*.exe

# The rclone program (downloaded binary) and the R2 credentials it uses.
# Credentials are secrets: they live here and never in git.
corpus-db/build/tools/
corpus-db/build/_secrets/
corpus-db/build/_logs/

# The restore test's working set: a copy of the record, the restored bytes
# (1.2 GB) and a second Meilisearch data directory. Runtime, rebuildable.
corpus-db/test_restore/

# Paper output from running the server: one .docx per generated document. The
# index.json beside them is tracked; the rendered files themselves are runtime
# output and are rebuilt on demand.
business_pipeline_v0.12/business_pipeline/documents/*.docx

# A hand-made backup of a source file while a change is in flight.
*.bak

# Attached student files: briefs, datasets and declared source lists, plus the
# JSON record written beside each one. This is the runtime attachment directory
# (BP_INTAKE_DIR, default <repo>/intake/). An upload is the student's own
# material, not source, so it stays out of git the same way the rendered papers
# in documents/ do.
business_pipeline_v0.12/business_pipeline/intake/

# Scratch measurement trees (never committed).
#
# The suite is measured against byte-exact copies of commits, and those copies
# are large: see business_pipeline_v0.12/business_pipeline/qa/manual/suite_measure.ps1
# and qa/manual/suite_treehash.py. They are evidence, not product, so they stay
# out of the repository.
#
# `.baseline_head/` is still tracked: it was committed by accident in e4184a8,
# and untracking it is the owner's call, not a side effect of this file.
.baseline_head/
.baseline_head2/
.baseline_pre/
.snapshot_wt/

# The session scratch directory: one-off scripts, suite logs and the byte-exact
# measurement archives. Two of the archives in it are 345 MB each, and GitHub
# refuses any blob over 100 MB, so a stray `git add -A` would fail the push
# outright. None of it is source: it is the working evidence of a build session.
.scratch/

# Cloudflare's local cache (the account id and the project name, nothing else).
# It is a cache of the deployment tool, not source.
.wrangler/
